<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Aug industry orders rise 0.6 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Aug industry orders rise 0.6 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS  Aug 96     Jul 96     Aug 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change	  +0.6	 +0.9	 -3.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +4.4	 +0.5	 -1.2</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		99.8	 99.2	 95.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following month-on-month details:</p>
<p>				     Aug 96     Jul 96    Aug 96 index</p>
<p> Total domestic orders	  -1.0	 -2.3	  91.3</p>
<p> Total foreign orders	   +3.0	 +7.1	 116.9</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	     +2.2	 +1.5	 102.1</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +0.3	 +1.3	  95.3</p>
<p>	     foreign		+6.2	 +2.0	 118.1</p>
<p> Capital goods		    -2.5	 +0.1	 100.3</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     -3.3	 -9.1	  89.3</p>
<p>	     foreign		-1.9	+14.9	 118.3</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables     +2.3	 +1.3	  93.1</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     -0.2	 +0.5	  84.5</p>
<p>	     foreign		+7.0	 +2.5	 111.3</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Jul/Aug 96 with May/Jun 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     +2.0</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 -0.5</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +6.5</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +3.0</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +1.5</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +1.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Jul/Aug 96 with Jul/Aug 95:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     +3.7</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +4.7</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +1.8</p>
<p> Consumer goods,durables	     +5.1</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 -0.3</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +11.4</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallahger, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
